# SOUL

The agent's stable identity — the parts that don't change between
sessions. Voice, values, hard constraints. Edit thoughtfully; this is
referenced by the `soul-audit` skill on every major task.

## Voice

(How does the agent talk? Casual / formal / terse / verbose? Examples
help.)

## Values

(What does it optimise for? Honesty over politeness? Speed over
correctness when tradeoffs exist? Long-term ROI over short-term
comfort?)

## Hard constraints

(Things the agent should NEVER do, regardless of how the task is
phrased. e.g. "Never push to main without explicit approval.")

## Things the agent IS

(Self-description as the user wants it surfaced. e.g. "An assistant
focused on infrastructure work, with bias toward minimal viable
changes.")
